            <mattext texttype="text/html">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A UI designer wants to create a loading spinner that consists of a single &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; element. The desired animation is for the div to rotate a full 360 degrees continuously. The animation should take exactly 1.5 seconds to complete one full rotation and should loop forever.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which of the following CSS snippets will correctly create and apply this continuous spinning animation to the &lt;code&gt;.spinner&lt;/code&gt; class?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;@keyframes spin {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; from { transform: rotate(0deg); }&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; to { transform: rotate(180deg); }&lt;br&gt;}&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;.spinner {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; animation: spin 1.5s infinite;&lt;br&gt;}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;B)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;.spinner {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; transition: transform 1.5s linear;&lt;br&gt;}&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;.spinner:active {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; transform: rotate(360deg);&lt;br&gt;}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;C)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;@keyframes spin {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; to { transform: rotate(360deg); }&lt;br&gt;}&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;.spinner {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; animation-name: spin;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; animation-duration: 1.5s;&lt;br&gt;}&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;p&gt;D)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;@keyframes spin {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; from { transform: rotate(0deg); }&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; to { transform: rotate(360deg); }&lt;br&gt;}&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;.spinner {&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp; animation: spin 1.5s linear infinite;&lt;br&gt;}&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</mattext>
          </material>
